{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4944d4de26b049c","type":"tool_result","content":"/workspace/pkg/github.go\n/workspace/pkg/github_test.go\n/workspace/pkg/steps_gh_token.go\n/workspace/pkg/steps_gh_token_test.go\n\n/workspace/pkg/githubauth:\nexport_test.go\ngithub_auth_setup.go\ngithub_auth_setup_test.go\ngithub_auth_tokenfile.go\ngithub_auth_tokenfile_test.go\ngithubauth_suite_test.go\n---\n# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\n\nThe format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),\nand this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).\n\n## v0.8.7\n\n- chore: remove orphaned section comments left in `.trivyignore` by the stale-ignore sweep\n\n## v0.8.6\n\n- chore: remove 10 stale vulnerability ignores (withdrawn advisory, module absent from go.mod, or version outside the affected range)\n\n## v0.8.5\n\n- fix: bump the baked dark-factory pin from `v0.199.6` to `v0.199.7`, which stashes the dirty spec bookkeeping around the branch workflow's `git merge origin/<default>` sync. `syncWithRemoteViaDeps` fetched and merged before `setupInPlaceBranch` persisted the generator's spec-status write, so `git merge` aborted with `Your local changes to the following files would be overwritten by merge: specs/in-progress/…`; the prompt failed permanently, the lifecycle drain aborted, and the agent exited 1 — surfaced as a bare `pod_crash_no_stdout`. `syncWithRemoteViaDeps` now stashes `SpecBookkeepingPrefixes` before the merge and pops after. Both the CLI build and the plugin marketplace clone move together, since they are pinned to the same `DARK_FACTORY_VERSION`.\n\n## v0.8.4\n\n- fix: bump the baked dark-factory pin from `v0.199.5` to `v0.199.6`, which approves a generated prompt set in the order the prompt-creator prefixed it. `diffFiles` ranged over the inbox snapshot map, and the auto-approve loop approves one prompt at a time — `ApproveFromInbox` strips the creator's prefix and `NormalizeFilenames` assigns the next free number — so execution numbers were assigned in Go's randomised map order. A spec declaring `service → route → hardening` came out `186-route` / `187-hardening` / `188-service`, running the hardening prompt before the service it exercises. `diffFiles` now sorts by the numeric prefix on each filename (parsed, so `10-` follows `2-`), unprefixed last, full path as the tie-break. Both the CLI build and the plugin marketplace clone move together, since they are pinned to the same `DARK_FACTORY_VERSION`.\n\n## v0.8.3\n\n- fix: bump the baked dark-factory pin from `v0.199.4` to `v0.199.5`, which carries the cross-branch stash fix. `brancher.StashInPaths` treated an empty `git status --porcelain` result as a tracked change — `strings.Split(\"\", \"\\n\")` yields `[\"\"]`, neither `??` nor `!!` — so every `SpecBookkeepingPrefixes` entry joined the `git stash push` pathspec and any bookkeeping dir the repo never created aborted the whole prompt setup with `pathspec ':(prefix:0)specs/rejected' did not match any file(s) known to git`. That killed the `bborbe/vault-ui` PR #232 cluster run on 2026-11-23T10:59Z. `StashInPaths` now returns early on an empty status, mirroring the guard `CommitUncommittedInPaths` already carried. Both the CLI build and the plugin marketplace clone move together, since they are pinned to the same `DARK_FACTORY_VERSION`.\n\n## v0.8.2\n\n- fix: bump the baked dark-factory pin from `v0.199.3` to `v0.199.4`, which carries the cross-branch spec-status write fix. A cluster run that starts on the default branch and must switch onto a PR branch now lands the spec-status write in the target branch's history (stash → switch → pop → commit) instead of refusing at branch setup with `working tree is not clean`. Both the CLI build and the plugin marketplace clone move together, since they are pinned to the same `DARK_FACTORY_VERSION`.\n\n## v0.8.1\n\n- fix: bump the baked dark-factory pin from `v0.198.11` to `v0.199.3`, which carries the spec-status write-before-branch-switch fix. The image bakes dark-factory at build time, so a release alone never reached the running agent — every cluster run kept executing the old refusal (`working tree is not clean; cannot switch to branch`) at branch setup. Both the CLI build and the plugin marketplace clone move together, since they are pinned to the same `DARK_FACTORY_VERSION`.\n\n## v0.8.0\n\n- fix: **`REPOS_PATH` and `WORK_PATH` are now required at startup instead of defaulting to the unwritable `/repos` and `/work`.** The pod runs as the image's unprivileged `node` user against a root-owned `/`, so an omitted variable resolved to an unwritable root and the run died minutes later at `git worktree add` with `fatal: could not create leading directories of '/work/<job>/.git': Permission denied` — 12 implement tasks hit it on prod between 2026-10-19 and 2026-11-02, and nothing in the failure named the variable. Both fields lose their `default:` tag and gain `required:\"true\"`, so the argument parser fails immediately with `Required field empty, define parameter work-path or define env WORK_PATH`. Both nuke stages already pin both variables, so no running deployment changes. `cmd/run-task` keeps its `~/.cache/github-dark-factory-agent/{repos,work}` fallback — that binary is the local CLI entry point, where a default is the point.\n\n## v0.7.2","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad01bb35-0bb9-465a-bce8-8503e77fa89d","uuid":"139d86f8-2097-4519-ae3e-98d741a34151","timestamp":"2026-11-27T12:45:43.752Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/workspace/pkg/github.go\n/workspace/pkg/github_test.go\n/workspace/pkg/steps_gh_token.go\n/workspace/pkg/steps_gh_token_test.go\n\n/workspace/pkg/githubauth:\nexport_test.go\ngithub_auth_setup.go\ngithub_auth_setup_test.go\ngithub_auth_tokenfile.go\ngithub_auth_tokenfile_test.go\ngithubauth_suite_test.go\n---\n# Changelog\n\nAll notable c